{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_011Cf6JbDc6eAphHmghi78eA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI've successfully added the GET `/api/tags/popular` endpoint. The implementation follows the existing three-layer architecture and patterns in this codebase.\n\n### Files Changed:\n\n1. **src/tags/tag.repository.ts** - Added `listPopular()` method to interface and implementation that queries the database for the top N tags ordered by article count descending\n\n2. **src/tags/tag.service.ts** - Added `listPopular()` method that delegates to the repository\n\n3. **src/tags/tag.routes.ts** - Added GET `/tags/popular` route handler that returns 10 most-used tags in the required JSON format: `{ \"tags\": [ { \"name\": \"<tag>\", \"count\": <number> } ] }`\n\nThe route is automatically registered via the existing `app.use(\"/api\", createTagRouter(tagService))` in app.ts, so it's reachable at `/api/tags/popular`. The implementation uses Prisma's `_count` and `orderBy` to efficiently get tag usage counts, follows the same error handling pattern as existing routes, and places the more specific route before the generic `/tags` route for proper Express routing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1560,"cache_read_input_tokens":38750,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1560},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0202dcd-1def-4422-acc7-dff6c438412b","uuid":"74db1a0e-1385-4ba7-ac20-bc6f58a095f0","timestamp":"2026-09-16T02:09:17.821Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6JbCsh1hrRtVW5irzBV"}
